{"id":"G3140","lemma":"μαρτυρέω","transliteration":"martureō","sayIt":"martureō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to testify","meaning":"μαρτυρέω, -ῶ\n(μάρτυς), [in LXX chiefly for עֵד (עֵד (Gen.31:47-48, al.), also for עוּד hi. (Gen.43:3, La 2:13), עָנָה (Num.35:30) ;]\n(a) prop., to be a witness, bear witness, testify: absol. (find., al.), Jhn.15:27, Act.26:5; parenthetical (Bl., § 79, 7; MM, xvi), 2Co.8:3; with dative of person(s) (comm. and incomm.; El., § 37, 2), Act.22:5, Heb.10:15; id. before ὅτι, Mat.23:31, Rom.10:2, al.; accusative and inf., Act.10:43; with accusative of thing(s) (cl.), Jhn.3:11, Rev.22:16, 20; with accusative cogn., before περί, Jhn.5:32, 1Jn.5:10; with dative of thing(s), Jhn.5:33, Act.14:3, al.; before περί, with genitive (of person(s) and of thing(s)), Jhn.1:7-8, 15 2:25 18:23 21:24, al.; id. before ὅτι, Jhn.5:36 7:7; ὅτι, Jhn.1:34 4:44 al.; ὅτι recit., Jhn.4:39; κατά before ὅτι, 1Co.15:15; pass., Heb.7:8; ptcp., Rom.3:21; impers., Heb.7:17;\n(b) in late Gk., to witness favourably, give a good report, approve (Bl., § 54, 3; MM, xvi; Deiss., BS, 265): with dative of person(s), Luk.4:22; before ἐπί with dative of thing(s), Heb.11:4; pass., Act.6:3; before ἐν, 1Ti.5:10, Heb.11:2; διά, with genitive of thing(s), Heb.11:39; with genitive of person(s), Act.10:22, al.; impers., III Jn 12 (cf. ἐπι, συν-επι-, κατα-, συν-μαρτυρέω)\n(AS)","glosses":["testify","testified","can testify","testifies","testimony","commended"],"count":72,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-23","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"you testify","kjv":"ye be witnesses"}},{"chapterId":"luk-4","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"spoke well","kjv":"bare"}},{"chapterId":"jhn-1","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"testify","kjv":"bear witness"}},{"chapterId":"jhn-1","v":8,"renderings":{"bsb":"he came to testify","kjv":"bear witness"}},{"chapterId":"jhn-1","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"testified","kjv":"bare witness"}},{"chapterId":"jhn-1","v":32,"renderings":{"bsb":"testified","kjv":"bare re